# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# scratch / backups
*.bak
_full.bak

# NOTE: experiments/out/ is intentionally tracked — the CSVs/PNGs/summary.md
# are paper deliverables (reproducible via `python -m experiments.run_synthetic`).
# The EICU_* artifacts that land there are aggregate-only BY CONSTRUCTION
# (run_eicu.assert_aggregate_only gates every write), so they stay tracked too.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# eICU-CRD v2.0 — the extract is NOT redistributable and MUST NOT be committed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PhysioNet Credentialed Health Data License 1.5.0 + DUA 1.5.0: the data require
# CITI training, a signed DUA and credentialed access, and they restrict DERIVED
# RECORD-LEVEL artifacts as well as the raw tables. Deny by default here for the
# same reason the feature allowlist does: a gitignore miss is unrecoverable once
# it is pushed.

# any gzipped CSV anywhere — an eICU table or a generated mock corpus is the
# only thing that shape can be in this repo; no deliverable is a .csv.gz
*.csv.gz
*.csv.bz2
*.csv.zip

# the released zip and the files that ship beside it
eicu*.zip
eicu-collaborative-research-database*/
SHA256SUMS.txt

# conventional extract / mock-corpus directories (eicu-mock, eicu_data,
# eicu-full, ...). Directory-only patterns, so experiments/eicu_etl.py and
# experiments/eicu_mock.py stay tracked.
eicu-*/
eicu_*/
*/eicu-*/
*/eicu_*/
/data/
/extract/

# record-level derivatives, wherever they land
*.eicu.npy
*.eicu.npz
EICU_records*
EICU_*_records.*
